define-telegram-commands-in-app-server

Lane: cross

Unit: send-notifications-through-telegram

ChildPatch: define-telegram-commands-in-app-server

Form: GitDiff

Segment: schema

Purpose: Configure Telegram delivery through the control center and notify about successful primary turns, live asynchronous questions, approval requests and new Codex releases.

Requires: Unit:cross/configure-application-proxy-at-runtime, Unit:cross/host-dialogs-with-shared-resources

Provides: Expose typed serialized telegram/command RPC, private atomic telegram.json storage, credential-redacted bounded delivery through shared runtime routing, independent staged masked dialog constructors using shared resources, setup that tests both services before saving, configurable release monitoring with a silent initial baseline, completion duration filtering, and successful-delivery deduplication for source-identified immediate notifications.

Boundary: Preserve native terminal notification settings and approval handling independently; do not notify for historical questions, failed or interrupted turns, secondary-thread completions, legacy input tools or plan prompts. Credentials stay out of UI results and transport diagnostics, failed probes never persist partial setup, background release checks stop on shutdown, and no legacy configuration or command reader is retained. Keep configuration business here and dialog resources in their cross infrastructure owner; expose settings without a private slash command, leaving control-center hosting, layout and shortcuts to its interface consumer.

Verification: Protocol command-shape and redaction tests, private store and HTTP mock tests, release baseline and cancellation tests, RPC setup and delivery tests, independent dialog setup and nested refresh tests, embedded TUI setup integration, and real event consumers covering primary completion, live and buffered questions, approvals, cancellation and exclusions.

CrossGroup: control-center


